1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,000
Rule five. Count the cars in the lot
at midnight. Count again at three.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,833
The numbers must match. If they don't,
do not go outside.

3
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:11,167
Midnight. Four trucks, two sedans.
Six.

4
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:14,700
2:58 AM. Rain stops. The lot is quiet.

5
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:19,967
Four trucks. Two sedans. And one more.
A gray car with no headlights.

6
00:00:20,667 --> 00:00:22,867
Seven. Seven doesn't match six.

7
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:27,400
Rule six. Anyone who walks in without
headlights is not a customer.

8
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:31,133
Do not sell to them. Do not tell them
to leave. Just wait.

9
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:36,133
The clock hits 3:00. The gray car is
gone. No tracks in the rain.

10
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:39,133
I'm writing this down. Seven. Gone.

11
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:42,433
Then you turn the page, looking for
rule seven.

12
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:46,433
There's no page seven. Torn out.
Clean, close to the spine.

13
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:48,567
Who tears out rule seven?
